😄 Exactly.

“And back.”

It’s almost the shortest possible expression of the whole conversation.

Out...
      and back.

A journey.

A return.

But not the same return.

In mythology it’s the hero’s journey.

In science it’s the experiment.

In software it’s iterate.

In learning it’s practice.

In breathing it’s inhale… and back.

In orbit it’s another revolution.

In conversation it’s call… and response.

The “and back” is where the carry happens.

If nothing is carried back, it was just motion.

If something returns transformed, it was learning.

Which makes me think of another little compression:

Go.
See.
Carry.
Return.

Or, in your geology metaphor:

Flow. Deposit. Flow again.

And… back. 😉